1
00:00:01,860 --> 00:00:03,150
Yuji.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,460
Hmm?

3
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:08,860
You're a strong kid, so help others.

4
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:21,550
Episode 41
Thunderclap, Part 2

5
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:26,560
23:05      Dogenzaka, In Front of Shibuya 109

6
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:27,720
In my Ten Shadows Technique,

7
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:31,820
only two Demon Dogs are 
granted to the user at first.

8
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:37,530
The other shikigami aren't granted to the 
user until they finish subjugating them.

9
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:44,750
The user must continue subjugating each one 
to increase the shikigami available to them,

10
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:49,400
until they are finally able to 
command all ten shikigami.

11
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:54,620
You done?

12
00:00:55,610 --> 00:00:59,820
You're really strong, 
just like that woman from earlier.

13
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:01,130
Even though you're young.

14
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:05,230
You're all beat up, yet you give 
me no openings to get close.

15
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:09,730
Though, with all that bleeding, 
I won't even have to do anything.

16
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:18,870
Thing is, this subjugation can 
be done with multiple people.

17
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:25,150
Though conducting the subjugation 
with multiple people voids it afterward.

18
00:01:25,150 --> 00:01:30,990
Which means the ritual becomes 
pointless to the sorcerer themselves.

19
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:37,000
Still, even if it is pointless, 
there are ways to use it.

20
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,020
Who's that?

21
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:43,280
They're being real flashy.

22
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:46,120
To continue,

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,870
while the shikigami can't be used 
without first subjugating it,

24
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:56,220
the user can summon them 
as many times as necessary

25
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,280
for the purpose of subjugating them.

26
00:01:58,780 --> 00:01:59,760
You don't mean...

27
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:04,880
In all of sorcerer history, there's never been

28
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:08,390
anyone who managed 
to subjugate this one.

29
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:13,500
Do you know why the Gojo clan 
and the Zen'in clan are on bad terms?

30
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:16,560
Are they actually on bad 
terms in the first place?

31
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:19,220
Sparks are constantly flying.

32
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:22,250
Since the Edo era? Or the Keicho era?

33
00:02:22,490 --> 00:02:23,880
I forget when,

34
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:29,140
but the heads of the clans at the time 
got serious during a spectated match,

35
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:30,880
and they both died.

36
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,380
Were the heads of those clans...

37
00:02:33,970 --> 00:02:39,150
One was someone like me who possessed both 
the Six-Eyes and the Limitless technique.

38
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:43,140
And the other used the same 
technique as you, Megumi.

39
00:02:44,990 --> 00:02:46,950
The Ten Shadows Technique.

40
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:52,600
Understand what I'm getting at?

41
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:57,970
That doesn't mean I can actually become 
a sorcerer capable of beating you.

42
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:03,740
I imagine the head of the clan used 
this in much the same way back then.

43
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:09,390
Sacred treasure swing and ring, ring.

44
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,720
Sukuna-sama?

45
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:16,200
Urgent business.

46
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:17,990
I see.

47
00:03:18,730 --> 00:03:23,160
It won't be much longer before I'm free.

48
00:03:23,790 --> 00:03:26,540
Do not slack on our preparations.

49
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,320
See you later, Uraume.

50
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,400
As you wish.

51
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:32,570
I'll be awaiting your return.

52
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:51,360
He tricked me!

53
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:53,900
He's starting that ritual!

54
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:58,180
And he's forcing me to participate 
in the damn thing with him!

55
00:03:58,810 --> 00:04:00,690
Eight-Grip Sword...

56
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,160
Divergent Sila Divine General...

57
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,160
Makora.

58
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:18,490
See you later.

59
00:04:19,030 --> 00:04:19,950
Yeah!

60
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:22,940
Sorry, Itadori.

61
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,970
Hey, you damn bastard!

62
00:04:26,460 --> 00:04:28,310
I'll be dying first.

63
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:30,160
Give it your best.

64
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:43,360
Wait!

65
00:04:43,850 --> 00:04:46,220
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

66
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:48,380
Oh, fuck you!

67
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,380
Damn it!

68
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,320
Wake up, you shitty sorcerer!

69
00:04:55,010 --> 00:04:58,060
The technique of the 
curse user Shigemo Haruta

70
00:04:58,060 --> 00:05:03,580
erases life's little daily miracles 
from his memory and stores them up.

71
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:07,250
That stock manifests as the
markings under his eyes,

72
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:10,850
and when he is faced with a threat 
to his life, one miracle is released.

73
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:20,660
However, he is unaware of this fact himself.

74
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:21,890
Huh?

75
00:05:28,770 --> 00:05:30,560
Suspended animation, huh?

76
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,540
I see.

77
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:37,490
So saving this piece of trash 
really was the right move.

78
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:42,660
He probably sucked this thing into 
the subjugation ritual along with him.

79
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:45,970
Once this trash dies, too, 
the ritual will be complete.

80
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:49,080
Then Megumi Fushiguro's death 
will be established, as well.

81
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:51,600
Don't die on me.

82
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:55,570
There are things I need you to do for me.

83
00:05:56,740 --> 00:05:58,760
U-Um...

84
00:05:58,760 --> 00:05:59,960
Silence.

85
00:06:02,550 --> 00:06:05,040
For Megumi Fushiguro to survive,

86
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:08,210
I'll have to defeat this 
shikigami as an outsider,

87
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:11,980
and nullify his subjugation ritual.

88
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:19,880
Time for a tasting, then.

89
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:27,950
JUJUTSU KAISEN

90
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:27,950
JUJUTSU KAISEN

91
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:53,690
Dissect.

92
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:12,160
That sword...

93
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:15,290
It's the Sword of Exorcism, 
specialized in combating cursed spirits.

94
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:20,080
It's packed with the same positive energy 
generated by a reverse cursed technique.

95
00:07:22,050 --> 00:07:23,800
If I was a cursed spirit,

96
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:27,120
that would have eliminated 
me on the first blow.

97
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:30,760
Tastes awful.

98
00:07:41,310 --> 00:07:42,200
You wanna go?!

99
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,020
Oh?

100
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:09,340
You did something, didn't you?

101
00:09:48,710 --> 00:09:50,040
What the hell?!

102
00:10:00,550 --> 00:10:02,600
Now that felt odd.

103
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:27,200
Again?!

104
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:00,440
What is that?!

105
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,360
Run!

106
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,600
Help us!

107
00:11:03,050 --> 00:11:04,180
We're falling!

108
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:23,690
Cursed energy?!

109
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:28,080
You've done it now!

110
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,910
You can see it!

111
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:06,570
You see my technique!

112
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,100
I knew it.

113
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:21,050
You're similar to Yamata no Orochi.

114
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:23,920
You follow my slices,

115
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:26,900
and attack with cursed energy...

116
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:30,050
Both started happening after 
that great wheel revolved.

117
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,990
The incantation of sacred treasures

118
00:14:32,990 --> 00:14:36,560
and that great wheel both represent 
perfect cycles and harmony.

119
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:40,570
Which suggests that this shikigami's ability

120
00:14:40,570 --> 00:14:43,060
is to adapt to anything and everything.

121
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:45,880
It's the ultimate late-throw 
rock-paper-scissors!

122
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:52,840
You might have defeated me 
in the state I was in back then.

123
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:01,720
Now you've fascinated me, Megumi Fushiguro!

124
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:06,620
Domain Expansion:

125
00:15:08,070 --> 00:15:10,110
Malevolent Kitchen.

126
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:20,790
Sukuna's Domain, Malevolent Kitchen,

127
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:23,520
is unlike others in that

128
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:26,560
it does not cut out a 
separate space with a barrier.

129
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:31,160
Manifesting an innate domain 
without sealing it in a barrier

130
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:35,500
is like trying to paint a picture 
in the air without a canvas.

131
00:15:36,270 --> 00:15:38,760
It's truly a divine feat.

132
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:43,980
To top it off, by adding a pact to 
allow its victims a path of escape,

133
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:46,550
it vastly increases the range of

134
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:50,470
its guaranteed-hit effect to 
a maximum 200-meter radius.

135
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:54,840
Though out of consideration for 
its effect on Megumi Fushiguro,

136
00:15:54,840 --> 00:16:00,430
he has currently restrained the effect to 
a 140-meter radius limited to the surface.

137
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:08,990
Anything?

138
00:16:08,990 --> 00:16:10,630
Nope. No signal.

139
00:16:10,630 --> 00:16:11,530
Same.

140
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:15,170
I don't think we need to 
worry that much, though.

141
00:16:15,170 --> 00:16:16,040
Huh?

142
00:16:16,570 --> 00:16:19,790
Remember the guy with the 
megaphone? He should be—

143
00:16:21,830 --> 00:16:24,700
Sukuna's slices are comprised of two types.

144
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:29,820
"Fillet" attacks things with cursed energy 
in the range of his guaranteed-hit effect.

145
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:32,550
"Dissect" attacks things 
without cursed energy.

146
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:37,020
Both rain down endlessly upon everything 
until Malevolent Kitchen disappears.

147
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:42,140
The only sure way to 
defeat Makora is to bury it

148
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:46,130
with the first use of an 
attack before it can adapt.

149
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:49,580
Fillet would have 
fulfilled those conditions,

150
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:51,830
but that wouldn't necessarily hold true

151
00:16:51,830 --> 00:16:55,080
if it had adapted to slices in general,

152
00:16:55,490 --> 00:16:58,460
rather than to Dissect.

153
00:17:16,950 --> 00:17:21,020
Makora was close to 
finishing its regeneration.

154
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:50,470
Fuga (Open).

155
00:18:42,710 --> 00:18:44,660
What are you looking at?

156
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:46,570
Begone.

157
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:55,700
E-Excuse me, then!

158
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:58,360
I really am lucky!

159
00:18:58,860 --> 00:18:59,960
For another day...

160
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:02,000
I survived!

161
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:06,590
Shigemo's stock of miracles

162
00:19:06,590 --> 00:19:10,580
had been exhausted in his 
battle with Kento Nanami.

163
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:16,220
Oh, it's nearly time.

164
00:19:19,630 --> 00:19:20,820
Fushiguro!

165
00:19:22,270 --> 00:19:24,840
I just saw Itadori for a moment...

166
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,580
No, was it Sukuna?!

167
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:31,480
23:14         Dogenzaka, In Front of Shibuya 109

168
00:19:35,350 --> 00:19:39,340
Hey, brat, be sure to savor this.

169
00:20:24,290 --> 00:20:26,050
Die!

170
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:28,640
Only me!

171
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:31,260
Only me!

172
00:20:32,130 --> 00:20:33,540
Die!

173
00:20:34,690 --> 00:20:36,400
Right now!

174
00:21:36,060 --> 00:21:37,430
I have to go.

175
00:21:39,310 --> 00:21:40,890
I have to fight.

176
00:21:49,900 --> 00:21:51,820
Otherwise, I'll just be...

177
00:21:53,250 --> 00:21:57,760
JUJUTSU KAISEN
Shibuya Incident

178
00:21:54,030 --> 00:21:55,910
a murderer.

179
00:23:52,690 --> 00:23:54,840
This has gotten really bad!

180
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:57,000
I'll count prime numbers to calm down.

181
00:23:57,000 --> 00:24:00,280
One, two, three... uh, nine...

182
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:01,690
You missed five and seven.

183
00:24:01,660 --> 00:24:02,810
Next time, "Right and Wrong."

184
00:24:01,790 --> 00:24:07,000
Next Episode
Right and Wrong

185
00:24:02,810 --> 00:24:04,650
You'll turn into a panda if you don't watch!

186
00:24:04,650 --> 00:24:06,420
You really are an animal...
